I do not fully know the complete schema of your tools directory, but I can outline the exact pattern to wire real-time web access into Step 1 (Local Deterministic Tool Execution) of our architecture.

To give me real-time web access across different sites, we need two deterministic tool handlers in the engine:
1. **`webSearch`** — To query live search engines (e.g., Tavily, Serper, or DuckDuckGo API) and return structured search results and URL links.
2. **`fetchWebPage`** — To fetch and extract plain text or HTML content directly from a target URL when deep content parsing is needed.

---

### Step 1: Create `src/engine/tools/webTools.ts`

Here is a clean implementation template for the tools:

```typescript
import axios from 'axios';

export interface SearchResult {
  title: string;
  url: string;
  snippet: string;
}

// 1. Live Web Search Tool
export async function executeWebSearch(query: string): Promise<SearchResult[]> {
  // Example using Tavily or Serper API
  const apiKey = process.env.SEARCH_API_KEY;
  if (!apiKey) {
    throw new Error('SEARCH_API_KEY is not configured in .env');
  }

  const response = await axios.post('https://api.tavily.com/search', {
    api_key: apiKey,
    query: query,
    search_depth: 'basic',
    include_answer: false,
    max_results: 5,
  });

  return response.data.results.map((r: any) => ({
    title: r.title,
    url: r.url,
    snippet: r.content,
  }));
}

// 2. Direct Web Page Fetcher Tool
export async function fetchWebPage(url: string): Promise<{ url: string; content: string }> {
  const response = await axios.get(url, {
    headers: { 'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64)' },
    timeout: 8000,
  });

  // Basic HTML text extraction (or use JSDom / Cheerio for clean text)
  const rawText = typeof response.data === 'string' ? response.data : JSON.stringify(response.data);
  const cleanText = rawText.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ').slice(0, 4000); // Truncate for prompt bounds

  return {
    url,
    content: cleanText,
  };
}
```

